  "businessSummary": "MetaphonePtBr is an open-source (MIT) .NET library published on NuGet that converts a single Brazilian Portuguese word into a stable phonetic token for fuzzy name/address/brand search. This is a full AI-guided rewrite as version 3.0.0 (current is 2.0.14) of the same package ID with intentional breaking changes and no obsolete shims, multi-targeting netstandard2.0 and net10.0, free to redesign the API and fix phonetic rules (based on the legacy README at github.com/crisbraatz/MetaphonePtBrOld). Success means full rule test coverage, automated NuGet publishing via GitHub Actions, high Stryker.NET mutation score, benchmarks at least as fast as 2.x, complete docs with a 2.x migration guide, and a brand-new icon and logo.",
